{"parentUuid":"69ccb375-8f4a-416e-80ec-e3c7ab15d5c9","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a13cf5eff78c9773b","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01KR9ogGFH2vLKEeNXF8BnsJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GjeGudRPY68ha9rEVT4JEP","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"NeurASP answer set programming neural network benchmark 2024"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7984,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"output_tokens":199,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7984},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":199,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7984,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7984,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caot3WwkdmrmW2AP4bHpK","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"dbe10e1e-6a60-45cb-8ac6-18eaa1cf63d8","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:59:50.147Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"dbe10e1e-6a60-45cb-8ac6-18eaa1cf63d8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a13cf5eff78c9773b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GjeGudRPY68ha9rEVT4JEP","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"NeurASP answer set programming neural network benchmark 2024\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"NeurASP: Embracing Neural Networks into Answer Set Programming | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/342796349_NeurASP_Embracing_Neural_Networks_into_Answer_Set_Programming\"},{\"title\":\"[2307.07700] NeurASP: Embracing Neural Networks into Answer Set Programming\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.07700\"},{\"title\":\"NeurASP: Embracing Neural Networks into Answer Set Programming\",\"url\":\"https://scite.ai/reports/neurasp-embracing-neural-networks-into-8GDkr00Q\"},{\"title\":\"NeurASP: Embracing Neural Networks into Answer Set Programming | NSF Public Access Repository\",\"url\":\"https://par.nsf.gov/biblio/10184165-neurasp-embracing-neural-networks-answer-set-programming\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - azreasoners/NeurASP · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/azreasoners/NeurASP\"},{\"title\":\"Figure 1 from NeurASP: Embracing Neural Networks into Answer Set Programming | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/NeurASP:-Embracing-Neural-Networks-into-Answer-Set-Yang-Ishay/8794f6169c693fb85c809bb663172d1277d11a83/figure/0\"},{\"title\":\"dblp: NeurASP: Embracing Neural Networks into Answer Set Programming.\",\"url\":\"https://dblp.org/rec/conf/ijcai/YangIL20.html\"},{\"title\":\"NeurASP: embracing neural networks into answer set ...\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.5555/3491440.3491683\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] NeurASP: Embracing Neural Networks into Answer Set Programming | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/NeurASP:-Embracing-Neural-Networks-into-Answer-Set-Yang-Ishay/e53beddcf3b79dd1f4673f126bbda6526039b2b8\"},{\"title\":\"NeurASP: Embracing Neural Networks into Answer Set Programming | IJCAI\",\"url\":\"https://www.ijcai.org/proceedings/2020/243\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found about NeurASP:\n\n## Overview\n\nNeurASP is a simple extension of answer set programs by embracing neural networks, providing a way to integrate sub-symbolic and symbolic computation by treating neural network output as probability distributions over atomic facts in answer set programs.\n\n## Key Capabilities\n\nNeurASP can make use of a pre-trained neural network in symbolic computation and improve the network's perception result by applying symbolic reasoning in answer set programming, while also training a neural network better by using ASP rules so that it learns from both implicit correlations in data and explicit complex semantic constraints.\n\n## Original Publication\n\nThe work was published at the 29th International Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence (IJCAI 2020). The original research was authored by Zhun Yang, Adam Ishay, and Joohyung Lee.\n\n## Benchmarks and Evaluation\n\nThe methodology was evaluated on classical symbolic reasoning benchmarks including Sudoku, Maze, pathfinding and preference learning, with experimental results demonstrating outstanding accuracy and logical consistency.\n\nNote: The search results show NeurASP was originally published in 2020. While the search query included \"2024,\" there don't appear to be specific 2024 benchmarks or updates mentioned in the current results. If you're looking for more recent 2024-specific information about NeurASP benchmarks, I could conduct an additional search.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"4a48dc7c-c0d5-4076-ac70-9b426e3d8b91","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:59:56.184Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dbe10e1e-6a60-45cb-8ac6-18eaa1cf63d8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"69ccb375-8f4a-416e-80ec-e3c7ab15d5c9","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a13cf5eff78c9773b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RWtr6pdkn2wiu2w151Lr5A","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"DeepProbLog neural symbolic 2024 2025 combinatorial optimization SAT\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"The DeepLog Neurosymbolic Machine Vincent Derkinderen∗, a Robin Manhaeve∗, a\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2508.13697\"},{\"title\":\"Deep Symbolic Optimization for Combinatorial Optimization: Accelerating Node Selection by Discovering Potential Heuristics\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2406.09740\"},{\"title\":\"Solving Combinatorial Optimization Problems with Deep Neural Network: A Survey\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciopen.com/article/10.26599/TST.2023.9010076\"},{\"title\":\"Under-Review for Neurosymbolic Artificial Intelligence 1–27, 2025\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.07122\"},{\"title\":\"A Comprehensive Review of Neuro-symbolic AI for Robustness, Uncertainty Quantification, and Intervenability | Arabian Journal for Science and Engineering | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s13369-025-10887-3\"},{\"title\":\"Neural combinatorial optimization: A tutorial - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0305054825001303\"},{\"title\":\"Deep Symbolic Optimization for Combinatorial Optimization: Accelerating Node Selection by Discovering Potential Heuristics | Proceedings of the Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference Companion\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3638530.3664128\"},{\"title\":\"Neurosymbolic Programming | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/356895111_Neurosymbolic_Programming\"},{\"title\":\"Scaling Neuro-symbolic Problem Solving: Solver-Free Learning of Constraints and Objectives\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2508.20978v2\"},{\"title\":\"Neural Networks for Combinatorial Optimization: A Review of More Than a Decade of Research | INFORMS Journal on Computing\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/ijoc.11.1.15\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found about DeepProbLog, neural-symbolic AI, and their connections to combinatorial optimization and SAT:\n\n## DeepProbLog and Neural-Symbolic AI\n\nDeepProbLog is a probabilistic logic programming language that incorporates neural predicates in logic programming with an underlying differentiable translation of logical reasoning. In DeepProbLog, a neural network can output a probability distribution over predicate values, and the logic program uses these as probabilistic facts to reason about high-level outcomes.\n\n## Recent Developments (2024-2025)\n\nThe search results reveal several important advances in neuro-symbolic AI during this period:\n\n1. **DeepLog Framework**: One can transition from DeepProbLog to a probabilistic fuzzy logic semantics by replacing the Boolean logic structure with a t-norm-based fuzzy logic structure, while keeping the rest of the formalization and computational procedures unchanged.\n\n2. **Symbolic-Neural Integration for Reasoning**: DeepProbLog and Scallop are frameworks that extend ProbLog and Datalog, respectively, to ensure that the symbolic component is differentiable.\n\n## Combinatorial Optimization and SAT\n\nThe search results connect neural-symbolic approaches to combinatorial optimization. Recent work proposes the first deep symbolic branching framework for B&B MILP solvers, leveraging deep symbolic regression to learn a symbolic branching policy. Additionally, hybrid approaches combine both deep learning and exact reasoning, with follow-up work extracting explicit logical rules from neural-symbolic systems.\n\nThe research community is actively developing methods that integrate neural learning with symbolic constraint satisfaction and optimization solving in 2024-2025.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"0e6e33f6-2513-4a0b-a792-573dbcb3a5de","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:59:57.192Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"69ccb375-8f4a-416e-80ec-e3c7ab15d5c9","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
