{"parentUuid":"6b663af9-5328-49ad-81b8-2186445f01fd","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a13cf5eff78c9773b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L4kN26h3WTuJyZBLctCr3k","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Logic Tensor Networks 2024 2025 packing placement combinatorial\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Quick design of feasible tensor networks for constrained combinatorial optimization – Quantum\",\"url\":\"https://quantum-journal.org/papers/q-2025-07-21-1799/\"},{\"title\":\"LTN: Logic Tensor Networks | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-39179-8_4\"},{\"title\":\"Logic Tensor Networks (LTN)\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/logictensornetworks/logictensornetworks\"},{\"title\":\"IOS Press Ebooks - Chapter 17. Logic Tensor Networks: Theory and Applications\",\"url\":\"https://ebooks.iospress.nl/volumearticle/58858\"},{\"title\":\"Logic Tensor Networks - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0004370221002009\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] Logic Tensor Networks | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Logic-Tensor-Networks-Badreddine-Garcez/76db1e8479ae91590bb6c9ef21e347775771978b\"},{\"title\":\"Logic Tensor Networks (LTNs)\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/logic-tensor-networks-ltns\"},{\"title\":\"Logic Tensor Networks\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2012.13635\"},{\"title\":\"Logic Tensor Networks Lecture 6\",\"url\":\"https://neurosymbolic.asu.edu/wp-content/uploads/sites/28/2023/03/Lecture06-LTN.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Quick design of feasible tensor networks for constrained ...\",\"url\":\"https://quantum-journal.org/papers/q-2025-07-21-1799/pdf/\"}]\n\nI've found relevant search results for your query on Logic Tensor Networks in the context of combinatorial optimization, packing, and placement problems.\n\nHere are the key findings:\n\n## Logic Tensor Networks Overview\n\nLogic Tensor Networks (LTN) is a neurosymbolic framework that supports querying, learning and reasoning with both rich data and rich abstract knowledge about the world, using a differentiable first-order logic language called Real Logic.\n\n## Recent 2024-2025 Research\n\nThe search results reveal active research in this area during 2024-2025, particularly focusing on tensor networks for combinatorial optimization:\n\n1. HOBOTAN: Efficient Higher Order Binary Optimization Solver with Tensor Networks and PyTorch was published in 2024.\n\n2. A Quantum-Inspired Tensor Network Algorithm for Constrained Combinatorial Optimization Problems was developed.\n\n3. Research on computing solution space properties of combinatorial optimization problems via generic tensor networks has been conducted.\n\n4. Inductive Construction of Variational Quantum Circuit for Constrained Combinatorial Optimization was published in IEEE Access in 2025.\n\n## Applications to Packing and Placement\n\nThe search results indicate that tensor networks are being applied to various combinatorial problems, though the specific results don't explicitly detail packing and placement applications. The referenced papers include work on traveling salesman problems and other combinatorial optimization challenges that could relate to placement problems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"1a76d875-cf4f-41a7-b94e-76d50a45de60","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:06.553Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6b663af9-5328-49ad-81b8-2186445f01fd","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0858b404-b27a-4a66-b248-aa2ca4c51576","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a13cf5eff78c9773b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01No2n2ECTCVbuY4HjHR88D7","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"neuro-symbolic AI survey 2025 review trustworthy verifiable\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A Comprehensive Review of Neuro-symbolic AI for Robustness, Uncertainty Quantification, and Intervenability | Arabian Journal for Science and Engineering | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s13369-025-10887-3\"},{\"title\":\"Neuro-Symbolic AI: A Foundational Analysis of the Third Wave’s Hybrid Core | by Greg Robison | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://gregrobison.medium.com/neuro-symbolic-ai-a-foundational-analysis-of-the-third-waves-hybrid-core-cc95bc69d6fa\"},{\"title\":\"Neurosymbolic AI for Safe and Trustworthy High-Stakes Applications[v1] | Preprints.org\",\"url\":\"https://www.preprints.org/manuscript/202511.1342\"},{\"title\":\"[2501.05435] Neuro-Symbolic AI in 2024: A Systematic Review\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.05435\"},{\"title\":\"Neuro-Symbolic methods for Trustworthy AI: a systematic review | Neurosymbolic Artificial Intelligence\",\"url\":\"https://neurosymbolic-ai-journal.com/paper/neuro-symbolic-methods-trustworthy-ai-systematic-review\"},{\"title\":\"Neuro-symbolic AI for auditable cognitive information extraction from medical reports | Communications Medicine\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s43856-025-01194-x\"},{\"title\":\"Surveying neuro-symbolic approaches for reliable artificial intelligence of things | Journal of Reliable Intelligent Environments | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s40860-024-00231-1\"},{\"title\":\"A Comprehensive Review of Neuro-symbolic AI for Robustness, Uncertainty Quantification, and Intervenability - R Discovery\",\"url\":\"https://discovery.researcher.life/article/a-comprehensive-review-of-neuro-symbolic-ai-for-robustness-uncertainty-quantification-and-intervenability/168a7439ddd53f44ab6400387a43a84b\"},{\"title\":\"Neuro-Symbolic Artificial Intelligence: A Task-Directed ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.ijcai.org/proceedings/2025/1157.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Neuro-symbolic artificial intelligence: a survey | Neural Computing and Applications | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00521-024-09960-z\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here are several recent comprehensive surveys and reviews on neuro-symbolic AI with focus on trustworthiness and verifiability:\n\n## Key 2025 Surveys\n\n**\"A Comprehensive Review of Neuro-symbolic AI for Robustness, Uncertainty Quantification, and Intervenability\"** (December 2025)\n\nThis comprehensive survey presents neuro-symbolic AI as a hybrid paradigm combining neural networks' learning capabilities with symbolic AI's reasoning strengths, through three foundational dimensions: robustness, uncertainty quantification, and intervenability. Neuro-symbolic systems offer enhanced interpretability, verifiability, and control, making them promising candidates for real-world deployment.\n\n**\"Neurosymbolic AI for Safe and Trustworthy High-Stakes Applications\"** (November 2025)\n\nThis paper introduces neurosymbolic AI as a hybrid paradigm combining data-driven neural networks with rule-based symbolic reasoning as a viable path toward trustworthy AI, providing built-in safety guardrails, robust reasoning abilities, and transparent decision traces.\n\n**\"Neuro-Symbolic AI in 2024: A Systematic Review\"** (January-April 2025)\n\nFrom an initial pool of 1,428 papers, 167 met inclusion criteria, with the majority of research concentrated in learning and inference (63%), logic and reasoning (35%), and knowledge representation (44%). However, explainability and trustworthiness are less represented (28%), with Meta-Cognition being the least explored area (5%).\n\nThese surveys collectively highlight the importance of neuro-symbolic AI for building trustworthy, verifiable, and interpretable AI systems, particularly in high-stakes domains like healthcare and autonomous systems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"770bc880-1cd2-4cd8-99c3-08be0168322d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:08.203Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0858b404-b27a-4a66-b248-aa2ca4c51576","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e7a9701d-9973-4da7-b618-c94b65c40ded","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a13cf5eff78c9773b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P7LMXibVwMj3WkvznkwpZ1","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"neural network learn CDCL branching heuristic SAT NeuroSAT 2024 sound\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Improving CDCL SAT Solving using Graph Neural Networks\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2110.14053\"},{\"title\":\"Published as a conference paper at ICLR 2024\",\"url\":\"https://export.arxiv.org/pdf/2110.14053\"},{\"title\":\"Enhancing Modern SAT Solver With Machine Learning Method | Proceedings of the Great Lakes Symposium on VLSI 2025\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3716368.3735251\"},{\"title\":\"[2110.14053] NeuroBack: Improving CDCL SAT Solving using Graph Neural Networks\",\"url\":\"https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2110.14053\"},{\"title\":\"NeuroBack: Improving CDCL SAT Solving using Graph Neural Networks\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2110.14053\"},{\"title\":\"NEUROBACK: IMPROVING CDCL SAT SOLVING USING ...\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=samyfu6G93\"},{\"title\":\"Published as a conference paper at ICLR 2019 NEURAL HEURISTICS FOR SAT SOLVING\",\"url\":\"https://rlgm.github.io/papers/32.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Boolean Satisfiability via Imitation Learning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2509.25411\"},{\"title\":\"NeuroCore: Guiding CDCL with Unsat-Core Predictions\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/331700435_NeuroCore_Guiding_CDCL_with_Unsat-Core_Predictions\"},{\"title\":\"Neural Approaches to SAT Solving: Design Choices and Interpretability\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2504.01173\"}]\n\nI've completed a web search for your query. Here are the main results I found:\n\n## Key Findings\n\nThe search results reveal several neural network approaches for learning CDCL branching heuristics and related SAT-solving techniques:\n\n### NeuroBack (2024)\nNeuroBack enhances phase selection heuristics in CDCL SAT solvers and captures static backbone information from satisfiable formulas using offline model inference. Once trained, the offline model inference allows NeuroBack to execute solely on the CPU, making it completely independent of GPU resources. This paper was published at ICLR 2024.\n\n### NeuroCore\nNeuroCore aims to make solving more effective especially for large-scale problems by enhancing the branching heuristic for CDCL using supervised learning to map unsat problems to unsat core variables. NeuroCore performs frequent online model inferences to tune predictions, though this online inference is computationally demanding.\n\n### NeuroSAT\nNeuroSAT was the first framework adapting a neural model into an end-to-end SAT solver, which was not intended as a complete SAT solver.\n\n### Recent Approaches (2024-2026)\nNeuroBack (Wang et al., 2024) improves phase initialization with GNNs, and recent work explores whether Transformers can learn solver behavior directly.\n\nThe search results focus on GNN-based approaches for improving CDCL solvers, but I did not find specific information about \"sound\" approaches in the context of your query.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"326e7ff7-acb0-4f9a-9638-73b1f05b2a13","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:09.277Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e7a9701d-9973-4da7-b618-c94b65c40ded","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
