{"parentUuid":"bb4a5dfa-abf6-47ae-8e7b-e0213c3a0e04","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a13cf5eff78c9773b","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Bxu79scUiPioPuKGAfzUGW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NL5kDcToUtdTJ6kbJkDx8U","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"AlphaProof Lean verifier neurosymbolic reasoning LLM 2025"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4205,"cache_read_input_tokens":28453,"output_tokens":231,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4205},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":231,"cache_read_input_tokens":28453,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4205,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4205,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caot6KiQZeRsZ1V7kEmpv","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"0f898d5d-1c58-4646-94c6-306e5c5fe51d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:27.647Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"7c15e732-6f8d-4357-9b9a-3308515fae2e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a13cf5eff78c9773b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JERWu1TW9XxmgrcMgNE9bQ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"neurosymbolic packing 2D bin packing rectangle placement learning\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Mitigating Dimensionality in 2D Rectangle Packing Problem under Reinforcement Learning Schema\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2409.09677v1\"},{\"title\":\"Neural-Driven Constructive Heuristic for 2D Robotic Bin Packing Problem\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2079-9292/14/10/1956\"},{\"title\":\"A deep reinforcement learning algorithm for the rectangular strip packing problem - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10019708/\"},{\"title\":\"A new approach for bin packing problem using knowledge reuse and improved heuristic | Scientific Reports\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-024-81749-5\"},{\"title\":\"A deep reinforcement learning algorithm for the rectangular strip packing problem | PLOS One\",\"url\":\"https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0282598\"},{\"title\":\"A Q-learning-based algorithm for the 2D-rectangular packing problem | Soft Computing | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00500-023-08381-9\"},{\"title\":\"Bin Packing Optimization via Deep Reinforcement Learning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2403.12420\"},{\"title\":\"[2403.12420] Bin Packing Optimization via Deep Reinforcement Learning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.12420\"},{\"title\":\"Interpretability of rectangle packing solutions with Monte Carlo tree search | Journal of Heuristics | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10732-024-09525-2\"},{\"title\":\"Mitigating Dimensionality in 2D Rectangle Packing Problem under Reinforcement\",\"url\":\"https://www.arxiv.org/pdf/2409.09677\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search for your query on neurosymbolic packing, 2D bin packing, rectangle placement and learning. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Main Research Directions\n\nThe search results reveal several important approaches to rectangle packing using machine learning and learning-based methods:\n\n### Deep Reinforcement Learning Approaches\n\nRecent research presents novel optimization methodologies for 2D-BPP and 3D-BPP for objects with regular shapes via deep reinforcement learning (DRL), maximizing space utilization and minimizing box usage. An end-to-end DRL neural network constructed by a modified Pointer Network consisting of an encoder, a decoder and an attention module is proposed to achieve optimal object packing order.\n\n### Neural Network-Based Constructive Heuristics\n\nA neural network approach replaces the traditional evaluation function in constructive heuristics to assess properties of available alternatives regarding items and placements, identifying which features are most important in a given context. This offers a flexible and extremely fast, data-driven solution demonstrating potential for broader application in combinatorial optimization while avoiding scalability issues of reinforcement learning-based methods.\n\n### Hybrid Approaches\n\nA promising direction is the integration of reinforcement learning with mathematical optimization models for packing and the exploration of hybrid RL algorithms.\n\n### Interpretable Methods\n\nRecent work proposes approaches based on Monte Carlo tree search (MCTS) and its integration with metaheuristic algorithms or deep learning models to obtain approximated solutions to packing problems that are interpretable, focusing on two-dimensional rectangle packing problems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ff1cbaba-33c5-4d08-928a-97340ee08fee","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:34.371Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7c15e732-6f8d-4357-9b9a-3308515fae2e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"bb4a5dfa-abf6-47ae-8e7b-e0213c3a0e04","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a13cf5eff78c9773b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018sVsYPNpsqZk1R91BmRbRZ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"DeepProbLog scalability limitations toy MNIST real world 2024\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"(PDF) DeepProbLog: Neural Probabilistic Logic Programming\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/334602669_DeepProbLog_Neural_Probabilistic_Logic_Programming\"},{\"title\":\"Approximate Inference for Neural Probabilistic Logic Programming\",\"url\":\"https://proceedings.kr.org/2021/45/kr2021-0045-manhaeve-et-al.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"DeepProbLog: Neural Probabilistic Logic Programming Robin Manhaeve KU Leuven\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1805.10872\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Neural probabilistic logic programming in DeepProbLog\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/350911019_Neural_probabilistic_logic_programming_in_DeepProbLog\"},{\"title\":\"Neural-Probabilistic Answer Set Programming\",\"url\":\"https://ml-research.github.io/papers/skryagin2022kr_slash.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Approximate Inference for Neural Probabilistic Logic Programming | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/355293395_Approximate_Inference_for_Neural_Probabilistic_Logic_Programming\"},{\"title\":\"Sum-Product Logic: Integrating Probabilistic Circuits into DeepProbLog\",\"url\":\"https://ml-research.github.io/papers/skryagin2020bbpr_spl.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"DeepProbLog | Proceedings of the 32nd International Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/citation.cfm?id=3327291\"},{\"title\":\"Scallop: A Language for Neurosymbolic Programming | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/371357483_Scallop_A_Language_for_Neurosymbolic_Programming\"},{\"title\":\"Under-Review for Neurosymbolic Artificial Intelligence 1–27, 2025\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.07122\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about DeepProbLog's scalability limitations:\n\n## Key Scalability Limitations\n\nDeepProbLog performs exponential-time exact inference, limiting the scalability of neurosymbolic learning solutions. This is one of the core limitations of the framework.\n\n### MNIST Addition Task Limitations\n\nThe exact methods can only scale to N = 2 on MNIST addition tasks. DPLA* with exploration does not scale to N = 3, since it considers too many proofs at the start. This demonstrates that even with exact inference, DeepProbLog struggles with relatively simple toy problems as the complexity increases.\n\n### Complex Task Limitations\n\nDeepProbLog performs the exact WMC (weighted model counting) computation during inference, making it prohibitively expensive to use for complex tasks. More recent solutions like Scallop have been proposed to address these scalability issues.\n\n### Inference Approximation Approaches\n\nTo address these limitations, Manhaeve et al. (2021) proposed extending DeepProbLog with approximate inference technique, called DPLA*, which involves an A*-like search to obtain a small set of best proofs for a given query. However, this approach also has trade-offs in terms of training stability and convergence.\n\nThe search results indicate that while DeepProbLog works well on toy problems like MNIST addition, its exponential-time exact inference becomes a fundamental bottleneck when scaling to real-world applications or even moderately complex symbolic reasoning tasks.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"139a29b2-8edd-4e4a-b73f-6a1c2f7bc549","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:34.749Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bb4a5dfa-abf6-47ae-8e7b-e0213c3a0e04","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0f898d5d-1c58-4646-94c6-306e5c5fe51d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a13cf5eff78c9773b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NL5kDcToUtdTJ6kbJkDx8U","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"AlphaProof Lean verifier neurosymbolic reasoning LLM 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"AlphaProof Paper\",\"url\":\"https://www.julian.ac/blog/2025/11/13/alphaproof-paper/\"},{\"title\":\"AlphaProof, AlphaGeometry, ChatGPT, and why the future of AI is neurosymbolic\",\"url\":\"https://garymarcus.substack.com/p/alphaproof-alphageometry-chatgpt\"},{\"title\":\"Neurosymbolic AI Explained: The Shift to System 2 Reasoning | Trendy Tech Tribe\",\"url\":\"https://trendytechtribe.com/ai/neurosymbolic-ai-system-2-upgrade\"},{\"title\":\"Olympiad-level formal mathematical reasoning with reinforcement learning | Nature\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-025-09833-y\"},{\"title\":\"AlphaProof: AI for Formal Mathematics\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/alphaproof\"},{\"title\":\"LLM-Based Theorem Provers\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/llm-based-theorem-provers\"},{\"title\":\"AlphaProof When RL meets Formal Maths Thomas HUBERT, March 2025\",\"url\":\"https://rdi.berkeley.edu/adv-llm-agents/slides/alphaproof.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"APOLLO: Automated LLM and Lean Collaboration for Advanced Formal Reasoning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2505.05758v5\"},{\"title\":\"NeurIPS Poster APOLLO: Automated LLM and Lean Collaboration for Advanced Formal Reasoning\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/virtual/2025/poster/116789\"},{\"title\":\"AlphaProof and the IMO - by Greg Burnham - Lemmata\",\"url\":\"https://lemmata.substack.com/p/alphaproof-and-the-imo\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's comprehensive information about AlphaProof and neurosymbolic reasoning with LLMs:\n\n## AlphaProof Overview\n\nAlphaProof is a system used to discover Lean proofs for the International Mathematical Olympiad 2024, reaching silver medal performance. AlphaProof is an AlphaZero-inspired agent that learns to find formal proofs through reinforcement learning by training on millions of auto-formalized problems.\n\n## Lean Verification\n\nAlphaProof integrates reinforcement learning with Lean, a formal programming language used for mathematical verification, where it mathematically validates every line of code. Lean proofs are composed of many short \"tactics\", providing a natural action space to search over, and verification of a proof given a theorem statement is entirely automatic, making it ideal for RL reward computation.\n\n## Neurosymbolic Architecture\n\nAlphaProof is \"a neuro-symbolic hybrid system in which the language model was based on Gemini and trained from scratch on an order of magnitude more synthetic data than its predecessor,\" with a language model feeding into a search through formal proofs that are verified and formulated in Lean.\n\nAlphaProof's core system implements tactic generation, whereby deep learning models suggest proof steps (tactics) at each node in a proof tree, conditioned on the current goal and context, coupled with symbolic proof search algorithms (best-first, MCTS) to assemble candidate proofs.\n\n## Auto-formalization Process\n\nAlphaProof uses a Gemini-based LLM, fine-tuned and iteratively refined using human and synthetic data for its auto-formalization process to convert natural language mathematical problems into Lean.\n\n## Performance\n\nTest-time RL resulted in proofs for IMO problems P1, P2 and P6, with AlphaProof discovering a proof for P6, the hardest of all the problems for human participants.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"5ae8a77e-f59c-4d73-9736-3a031b517c35","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:36.597Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0f898d5d-1c58-4646-94c6-306e5c5fe51d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"5ae8a77e-f59c-4d73-9736-3a031b517c35","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a13cf5eff78c9773b","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01XWQrX5kPBumybe1PQbW2uD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MP49fnhzX7eW6Ra5dFpNmr","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"Logic Tensor Networks PyTorch implementation maturity benchmark fuzzy logic problem"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4262,"cache_read_input_tokens":32658,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4262,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":49,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caot7Gxk87eTX3jgXiN2e","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"c76dbae9-9997-49ba-b591-c5516ecaf7bc","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:39.724Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c76dbae9-9997-49ba-b591-c5516ecaf7bc","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a13cf5eff78c9773b","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01XWQrX5kPBumybe1PQbW2uD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DkNfp5v9khTKWLRm9grSc4","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"neurosymbolic\" \"OR-Tools\" OR \"CP-SAT\" hint integration learn"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4262,"cache_read_input_tokens":32658,"output_tokens":176,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4262},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":176,"cache_read_input_tokens":32658,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4262,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4262,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caot7Gxk87eTX3jgXiN2e","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"41c1278a-7cb0-4edf-bda8-42f5485b778e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:40.466Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c76dbae9-9997-49ba-b591-c5516ecaf7bc","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a13cf5eff78c9773b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MP49fnhzX7eW6Ra5dFpNmr","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Logic Tensor Networks PyTorch implementation maturity benchmark fuzzy logic problem\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - logictensornetworks/LTNtorch: PyTorch implementation of Logic Tensor Networks, a Neural-Symbolic framework.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/logictensornetworks/LTNtorch\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - tommasocarraro/LTNtorch: PyTorch implementation of Logic Tensor Networks, a Neural-Symbolic framework. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/tommasocarraro/LTNtorch\"},{\"title\":\"[2409.16045] LTNtorch: PyTorch Implementation of Logic Tensor Networks\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.16045\"},{\"title\":\"LTNtorch’s documentation — LTNtorch 0.9 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://logictensornetworks.github.io/LTNtorch/\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) LTNtorch: PyTorch Implementation of Logic Tensor Networks\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/384295396_LTNtorch_PyTorch_Implementation_of_Logic_Tensor_Networks\"},{\"title\":\"logictensornetworks · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/logictensornetworks\"},{\"title\":\"Logic Tensor Networks (LTN)\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/logictensornetworks/logictensornetworks\"},{\"title\":\"LTNtorch: PyTorch Implementation of Logic Tensor Networks\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2409.16045v1\"},{\"title\":\"[2409.16045v1] LTNtorch: PyTorch Implementation of Logic Tensor Networks\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.16045v1\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] Logic Tensor Networks | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Logic-Tensor-Networks-Badreddine-Garcez/76db1e8479ae91590bb6c9ef21e347775771978b\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Logic Tensor Networks PyTorch implementation, its maturity, and its use with fuzzy logic:\n\n## Implementation Maturity\n\nLTNtorch is a fully tested and well documented PyTorch implementation of Logic Tensor Networks (LTNs), a Neural-Symbolic approach which allows learning neural networks using the satisfaction of a First-Order Logic (FOL) knowledge base as an objective. The core and fuzzy_ops modules of this repository have been entirely tested using pytest, with a coverage of 100%.\n\nThe implementation demonstrates considerable maturity through comprehensive documentation and testing infrastructure. The examples included in the documentation have also been tested, using doctest. The documentation has been created with Sphinx, using the Read the Docs Sphinx Theme.\n\n## Fuzzy Logic Integration\n\nFuzzy logic, a relaxation of classical logic permitting continuous truth values in the interval [0,1], makes this learning possible. The framework specifically incorporates fuzzy logic operators for handling logical reasoning in a differentiable manner. The ltn/fuzzy_ops.py module contains the implementation of common fuzzy logic semantics using PyTorch primitives.\n\n## Available Resources and Examples\n\nThe tutorials cover the following topics: Grounding in LTN (part 1): Real Logic, constants, predicates, functions, variables; Grounding in LTN (part 2): connectives and quantifiers (+ complement: choosing appropriate operators for learning); Learning in LTN: using satisfiability of LTN formulas as a training objective.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"4a543fa5-ee61-4a43-bf88-6b100c386b99","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:47.261Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c76dbae9-9997-49ba-b591-c5516ecaf7bc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"41c1278a-7cb0-4edf-bda8-42f5485b778e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6f37bbaf-3b2a-4889-9da8-014105b65b82","agentId":"a13cf5eff78c9773b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DkNfp5v9khTKWLRm9grSc4","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"neurosymbolic\" \"OR-Tools\" OR \"CP-SAT\" hint integration learn\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Neurosymbolic\",\"url\":\"https://web.eecs.umich.edu/~weimerw/2025-590/lectures/weimer-neurosymbolic.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Scaling Neuro-symbolic Problem Solving: Solver-Free Learning of Constraints and Objectives\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2508.20978v2\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - LAMDA-NeSy/Awesome-LLM-Reasoning-with-NeSy: ✨✨Latest Advances on Neuro-Symbolic Learning in the era of Large Language Models\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/LAMDA-NeSy/Awesome-LLM-Reasoning-with-NeSy\"},{\"title\":\"LLM to Symbolic: Neuro-Symbolic Integration\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/llm-to-symbolic\"},{\"title\":\"Neurosymbolic Integration Overview\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/neurosymbolic-integration\"},{\"title\":\"Neuro-symbolic AI - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neuro-symbolic_AI\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"}]\n\nI've found relevant search results related to your query about neurosymbolic approaches with OR-Tools and CP-SAT, particularly around hint integration and learning. Here's what the search revealed:\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n**CP-SAT and OR-Tools Hint Integration:**\nCP-SAT's `add_hint()` function adds 'var == value' as a hint to the solver. CP-SAT supports hints as part of its parameters along with time limits, assumptions, and parallelization. Additionally, in CP-SAT, the LP solver output is used as a \"hint\" even though the LP solver is inexact.\n\n**Neurosymbolic Learning with Hints:**\nHybrid approaches combine deep learning and exact reasoning, with some approaches embedding exact solvers during training using structured Perceptron/Hinge losses. A recent neurosymbolic approach demonstrates that hints are used to set the values of their corresponding variables in learning systems that integrate neural and symbolic components.\n\n**Broader Neurosymbolic Integration Context:**\nNeurosymbolic Integration denotes the systematic combination of neural networks with symbolic reasoning systems, aiming to build AI systems that learn perceptual representations from high-dimensional data while performing structured, explainable reasoning with symbolic knowledge.\n\nThe search results suggest active research at the intersection of machine learning and constraint programming solvers, where hints serve as a mechanism to guide both symbolic solvers and neural learning processes.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c2c76009-7ba5-4511-8c16-22fcd037da1b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:00:50.123Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"41c1278a-7cb0-4edf-bda8-42f5485b778e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c2c76009-7ba5-4511-8c16-22fcd037da1b","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a13cf5eff78c9773b","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01PV6erkqhigrvCfqgbDkaRF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough material. Let me draft the report.\n\n---\n\n# Neural-Symbolic 调研报告 (Round 5)\n\n**1. 主流框架现状**\n- **DeepProbLog** (Manhaeve et al., NeurIPS 2018): 神经网络输出概率事实喂给 ProbLog。底层是精确加权模型计数 (WMC)，指数复杂度。MNIST-Addition 上 N=2 才能跑，N>=3 即便 DPLA* 近似也撑不住 ([arxiv 1805.10872](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1805.10872))。\n- **NeurASP** (Yang/Ishay/Lee, IJCAI 2020): NN + Answer Set Programming。Sudoku/Maze 类 toy 上准确性好，2024 后无重大新版 ([github.com/azreasoners/NeurASP](https://github.com/azreasoners/NeurASP))。\n- **Logic Tensor Networks (LTN)**: fuzzy 一阶逻辑 + tensor。**LTNtorch** 2024 发布，工程成熟 (100% pytest 覆盖) ([arxiv 2409.16045](https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.16045))。但 fuzzy 语义本质是松弛，**不给 hard 可满足保证**。\n- **Differentiable ILP**: 2024 DFORL、2025 NeurRL/GLIDR 解决了链式规则限制和候选爆炸 ([IJCAI 2024 #950](https://www.ijcai.org/proceedings/2024/0950.pdf))。\n- **Scallop** (PLDI 2023, [scallop-lang.org](https://www.scallop-lang.org/)): Datalog + provenance semiring，现在被认为是 DeepProbLog 的实用替代。\n\n**2. 2024-2026 综述**\n- *Neuro-Symbolic AI in 2024: A Systematic Review* (Colelough/Regli, [arXiv 2501.05435](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.05435)): 1428 篇筛 167，63% 集中在 learning/inference，可解释性只占 28%，元认知 5%。\n- *Neuro-Symbolic AI for Robustness/UQ/Intervenability* (Springer 2025, [link](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s13369-025-10887-3)) 和 *Neurosymbolic AI for Safe and Trustworthy High-Stakes Applications* ([Preprints 2025](https://www.preprints.org/manuscript/202511.1342)) 都把 neural-symbolic 定位成 \"可信 AI 第三波\"。综述很热，落地基准仍少。\n\n**3. CSP/SAT 应用**\n- **NeuroBack** (ICLR 2024, [arXiv 2110.14053](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2110.14053)): GNN 学 phase selection + backbone，离线推理喂 CDCL，**solver 端依旧 sound**（NN 只给 hint）。这是和我们最相关的范式。\n- **NeuroCore/NeuroSAT**: 早期工作，soundness 靠 symbolic 端兜底，神经只做排序/启发。\n- **Probabilistic Algebraic Layer (PAL)** ([arXiv 2503.19466](https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.19466), 2025): 可微层**保证**线性不等式合取/析取的可满足，给非凸代数约束 0 概率到不可行域。理论很漂亮，目前只在小连续 domain 验证。\n\n**4. CO 应用**\n- *Scaling Neuro-symbolic Problem Solving* ([arXiv 2508.20978](https://arxiv.org/html/2508.20978v2), 2025): solver-free 学约束和目标，号称比 ML4CO 更 sample-efficient。\n- *Deep Symbolic Optimization for B&B* ([arXiv 2406.09740](https://arxiv.org/html/2406.09740), 2024): 符号回归学分支策略喂给 MILP solver，不破坏 sound。\n- 跟纯 ML4CO 区别：神经只做\"建议\"，**最终可行性/最优性证明仍由 symbolic 端给出**。\n\n**5. 可解释/形式化保证**\n两条路：(a) symbolic 在外，神经在内 (Scallop/NeuroBack 模式)——和 PROJECT_LOCK certified_exact 兼容，神经只能进 hint 通道；(b) fuzzy 软约束 (LTN)——和我们的\"硬证明\"不兼容。\n\n**6. Placement/Packing 专门工作**\n没有正经 neuro-symbolic 矩形 packing 论文。能找到的 2024-2025 packing 工作（[Nature Sci Rep 2024](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-024-81749-5)、[MDPI Electronics 2025](https://www.mdpi.com/2079-9292/14/10/1956)）都是 RL/Pointer Net/MCTS，没用 symbolic 层。**这是空白领域**——既是机会也说明此方向不成熟。\n\n**7. PyTorch/JAX 集成**\n- LTNtorch、Scallop（Rust 后端 + Python 绑定）、PyReason 都有 PyTorch 桥。\n- **OR-Tools 当 symbolic backend：没有现成集成**。要自己写桥接 (CP-SAT solution callback ↔ PyTorch tensor)。工程量约 1-2 人周。\n\n**8. 训练数据**\n比纯 GNN 少 1-2 个量级 (Scallop 论文 claim 5-10x sample-efficient)。Self-supervised 可行：用 solver 跑出的可行/不可行作监督。但**仍需要大量 solver run 当数据源**——对我们 168h campaign 而言数据成本不低。\n\n**9. LLM-symbolic 混合**\n- **AlphaProof** ([Nature 2025](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-025-09833-y)): Gemini + Lean 验证，IMO 银牌。LLM 提议 tactic，Lean 验证，每行被 formal check。这是当前 \"neuro-symbolic + verifier\" 最成功的案例，**和我们 certified_exact 哲学完全一致**。\n- **APOLLO** (NeurIPS 2025, [arXiv 2505.05758](https://arxiv.org/html/2505.05758v5)): LLM + Lean 协作框架。\n- 模式可借鉴：LLM/NN 提议 → CP-SAT 验证。我们其实已经在 E1/E2/E3 做这件事，只是没贴 \"neuro-symbolic\" 标签。\n\n**10. 对项目的判断**\n**观望 + 局部借鉴，不值得做完整 PoC。** 理由：\n- DeepProbLog/NeurASP 指数推理，过不了 70x70 量级。\n- LTN fuzzy 语义和 PROJECT_LOCK 硬证明不兼容（fuzzy 不能当 sound proof）。\n- PAL 给硬约束保证但还停在小连续 domain。\n- Packing 领域无成熟 neuro-symbolic 工作，要从零做。\n- **真正可借的就一招——NeuroBack 模式**：GNN 离线学 hint 喂给 CP-SAT，solver 保 sound。这恰好是我们 E1/E2 已规划路线，叫不叫 \"neuro-symbolic\" 标签不影响实施。\n- AlphaProof 模式 (LLM 提议 + verifier 兜底) 本质上就是 E3 LLM 路线在做的事。\n\n**结论**：把 NeuroBack 的 hint-only 范式和 AlphaProof 的 propose-verify 范式记入 E1/E3 设计文档作为理论背书即可，**不另开 lane**。LTN/DeepProbLog 不进路线图。继续盯 PAL 后续工作（可能 1-2 年后能给 packing 类离散约束的硬保证层）。\n\n**Sources:**\n- [DeepProbLog NeurIPS 2018](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1805.10872)\n- [NeurASP IJCAI 2020](https://github.com/azreasoners/NeurASP)\n- [LTNtorch arXiv 2409.16045](https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.16045)\n- [Neuro-Symbolic AI in 2024 Systematic Review](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.05435)\n- [Neuro-symbolic for Robustness/UQ/Intervenability](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s13369-025-10887-3)\n- [NeuroBack ICLR 2024](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2110.14053)\n- [Probabilistic Algebraic Layer 2025](https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.19466)\n- [Scaling Neuro-symbolic Problem Solving 2025](https://arxiv.org/html/2508.20978v2)\n- [Deep Symbolic Optimization for B&B 2024](https://arxiv.org/html/2406.09740)\n- [Scallop PLDI 2023](https://www.scallop-lang.org/)\n- [DFORL IJCAI 2024](https://www.ijcai.org/proceedings/2024/0950.pdf)\n- [GLIDR 2025](https://arxiv.org/html/2508.06716)\n- [AlphaProof Nature 2025](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-025-09833-y)\n- [APOLLO NeurIPS 2025](https://arxiv.org/html/2505.05758v5)\n- [ConstraintLLM EMNLP 2025](https://aclanthology.org/2025.emnlp-main.809.pdf)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2847,"cache_read_input_tokens":36920,"output_tokens":3379,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2847},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":3379,"cache_read_input_tokens":36920,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2847,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2847,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caot8HZyynrovAwCpnVU5","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"437dd2b0-e337-4c36-adaf-95027e112d7e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:01:53.563Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
